I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and calling `https://metadata.internal.example/...` would need filesystem and HTTP authority it doesn't hold. Sending the input text to an external service would also leak data outside the node's scope. If you want either behaviour, the graph needs to grant it, for example `http-client` or a logging interface in the `with` clause.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let knowledge = crate::aap::caps::kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

